  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "⚔️ World of Warcraft Orc Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Orc names that fit in the character box, with a surname or clan for the story behind them."
    },
    "intro": "A World of Warcraft orc needs a name that sounds like the Horde, fits the game's rules and isn't already taken on your realm. This **WoW orc name generator** gives you names that do all three, male and female, plus an earned surname or a clan if you want a story to go with it: <em>Rokgath Ashbrand</em>, <em>Magira of the Frostwolf clan</em>.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Fitting the name into the game",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>2 to 12 letters, no spaces.</strong> The name you type at character creation is one word. Surnames and clans are for your profile, role-play addons and your own head-canon.</li><li><strong>No three of the same letter in a row.</strong> The game rejects names like <em>Grommm</em>. Every name in the \"fits in game\" format follows both rules.</li><li><strong>One per realm.</strong> If the name's taken, the game will tell you. Generate a batch and keep a few backups.</li><li><strong>Accents.</strong> Players often add an accent to get round a taken name (<em>Rókgath</em>). It works, but makes you harder to whisper.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
